   "value": "subject_definitions:\n<Subject 1> is a 32-year-old Italian woman, lighthouse keeper, with short tousled copper-red hair, light freckles, green-grey eyes, a bright yellow rain jacket over a grey wool sweater, dark jeans and black rubber boots. Facial identity from <Picture 0>; body, hair and wardrobe from the character sheet <Picture 1>.\n<Subject 2> is a windswept stone pier at the foot of a white lighthouse on a rocky Ligurian coast, grey-blue sea with white foam, overcast late-afternoon light.\n\nsummary:\n[reference generation] Two shots of <Subject 1> at <Subject 2>: a close-up where she speaks to the lens, then a wide full-length shot where she walks toward the camera and finishes the sentence.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Subject 1> (appears in [Shot 1], [Shot 2]): fully_preserved - face from <Picture 0>, hair, wardrobe and build from <Picture 1>.\n<Subject 2> (appears in [Shot 1], [Shot 2]): fully_preserved - the location, its light and its colours.\n\ndetailed_description:\nThe target video is a realistic, cinematic live-action short film, natural colours, fine film grain, shot on a 35mm cinema camera.\n[Shot 1] A close-up of <Subject 1> (S1), face filling a third of the frame, a windswept stone pier at the foot of a white lighthouse on a rocky Ligurian coast softly out of focus behind. She looks out to sea, then turns to the lens and says: <d>[English] The storm is coming.</d> The camera holds still with a very slight handheld drift.\n[Shot 2] A wide full-length shot of <Subject 1> (S1), whole figure from head to toe with space above and below, at <Subject 2>. She walks along the pier toward the camera, the lighthouse behind her, wind tugging at her jacket, and says: <d>[English] I'll keep the light on tonight.</d> The camera slowly dollies backward, keeping her centred.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nWind gusts, waves breaking on the rocks, gulls, the creak of a metal railing.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nNone.\n"
